1
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:18,180
The idea of the family is important all over the world and many countries have special occasions to celebrate it.

2
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:20,108
Let’s look at a few.

3
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:30,420
In Germany, the first day at school is a very important time for all children.

4
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,226
There is a special event called an Einschulung.

5
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:41,947
Everyone in the family meets to give the child presents, like pens and books, for their new school life.

6
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:49,528
For the first day of school, parents give their children a large paper cone called a Schultüte.

7
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:53,280
Inside there are things for school and sweets.

8
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:03,980
In traditional Japanese houses you often find a butsudan.

9
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:09,800
A butsudan is a special place where you go to remember your dead relatives.

10
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:18,832
People usually put things on the butsudan for their ancestors: a book, some flowers or a bowl of rice, for example.

11
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:25,438
Adults also tell stories about these people to their children so they are not forgotten.

12
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:34,215
Pets are popular in many cultures around the world.

13
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:38,700
Looking after an animal helps a child learn how to be responsible.

14
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:45,337
Every year in India there is a Hindu festival called Thai Pongal.

15
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:51,967
During the festival families feed cows and birds to give thanks for these animals.

16
00:01:52,940 --> 00:01:59,165
Children also learn that all living things are connected and must share the world together.

17
00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:10,043
In the Netherlands people celebrate the winter holiday on the 5th December.

18
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:13,352
This holiday is called Sinterklaas.

19
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:19,064
People give each other presents, but they also have a very special tradition.

20
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:25,438
Each member of the family writes their name on a piece of paper and puts it in a hat.

21
00:02:26,460 --> 00:02:31,429
Everyone then takes a name from the hat and writes a poem about this person.

22
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:35,820
Everyone sits in a circle and reads out their poems.
